# Work tracking

`WIP/` is a first-class dated corpus on `main`. It is committed, inventoried,
and pruned only when high-evidence shows the same bytes already live outside
`WIP/`. Git history is the undo.

## MUST

- Prefer new drops under `WIP/<M-D-YY>/<topic>/` (example: `WIP/8-16-26/`).
- Named series (`WIP/CG/`, packs) are allowed; inventory marks `kind: series`.
- Run `make wip-hygiene` (or `python3 ops/scripts/wip_corpus.py hygiene`) to
  file loose root files, refresh `WIP/INVENTORY.yaml`, and prune landed copies.
- Stage `WIP/**` with **explicit pathspecs only** (rule 49). Never `git add -A`.
- Maintain `TODO.md` as the agent task queue. One task per line. Status prefix
  required: `[ ]` open, `[~]` in progress, `[x]` done, `[!]` blocked.
- Include a Linear identifier when work spans sessions.

## MUST NOT

- Park `WIP/**` under `/tmp` or `.l9/scratch-hold/` to clean `make pr`.
- Recreate `current_work/` (retired). Leftovers go to `WIP/` or `TODO.md`.
- Track or stage `WIP/Legal Defense/` or credential-shaped WIP globs
  (`*oauth*.json`, `*credentials*.json`, `*client_secret*.json`).
- Prune unique or unmatched WIP. Auto-prune requires same sha256 on a tracked
  non-WIP path, or an explicit `landed:` inventory marker, plus a receipt
  under `WIP/_receipts/`.
- Treat `l9-git-work-preserve` as this contract — that skill inventories git
  refs/stashes and still never auto-deletes branches.
